# What does NOT go to the CDN.
#
# The deployed site is one static page (map/index.html) plus the tract-level
# data it fetches. Everything else in this repository exists for reproduction
# and review on GitHub, not for serving.

# Local environment and build detritus
venv
.git
.env
.vercel
.claude
.DS_Store
scripts/__pycache__

# Pipeline source. The map is a self-contained Leaflet page with no build step,
# so nothing here is needed at runtime. Reproduction happens from the repo.
scripts
.github
requirements.txt
refresh.sh
.gitattributes

# Working drafts. Their numbers no longer all match the final manuscript, and
# they should not be served next to a published preprint.
report.md
insights.md

# Candidate identifiability. These name 5,428 real businesses, with street
# addresses and exact coordinates, ranked as naloxone placement targets; none
# of those owners has been contacted. They stay in the repository so the
# ranking is reproducible, but the deployed map reads the tract-aggregated
# copies under data/public/ instead. See scripts/build_public_data.py.
data/clean/placement_candidates.csv
data/clean/placement_candidates.geojson
data/clean/placement_candidates_meta.json
data/clean/placement_ranked.csv
data/clean/placement_ranked.geojson
data/clean/placement_ranked_meta.json

# Upstream inputs and large intermediates the map never fetches.
data/raw
data/clean/block_access.csv
figures/*.pdf
